# Telemetry float precision

Human-readable mission telemetry floats use **exactly two decimal places**.

## Required

| Surface | Correct | Forbidden |
|---------|---------|-----------|
| `Telemetry_SendSensors` format | `%.2f` for T/P/H/Accel/Gyro and Magneto **magnitude** | `%.1f`, `%f`, `%.3f`, `%g` |
| Threshold / heading `Telemetry_Printf` floats | `%.2f` | `%.1f` |
| VESPER virtual-board sensor lines (`Command/src/sim.js`) | `.toFixed(2)` | `.toFixed(1)` |
| VESPER HUD sensor formatters (`Command/src/bindings.js` `fmt` / `vec`) | `.toFixed(2)` | `.toFixed(1)` |
| Contract / fixture examples of `Telemetry ->` | two d.p. (e.g. `26.40`) | one d.p. (e.g. `26.4`) |

## Out of scope

- Integer fields (charge `n/50`, countdown ms, mode tags) stay unscaled integers.
- `EVT RADAR` `az` / `pan` remain one decimal as documented in the radar contract.

If a diff or fixture regresses sensor-line precision to one decimal place, restore two d.p. before finishing.
